Task 2: Provision a VM from the Template
Subtask 2.1: Generate SSH Key Pair
First, generate an SSH key pair for secure access to your VMs:

# Generate SSH key pair
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -f ~/.ssh/vm-lab-key -N ""

# Display the public key
cat ~/.ssh/vm-lab-key.pub
Note: Copy the public key output as you'll need it for VM provisioning.

Subtask 2.2: Provision Ubuntu VM from Template
Create your first VM using the Ubuntu template:

# Set your SSH public key as a variable
export SSH_PUB_KEY="$(cat ~/.ssh/vm-lab-key.pub)"

# Process the template and create the VM
oc process ubuntu-basic-vm-template \
  -p VM_NAME=ubuntu-web-server \
  -p CPU_CORES=2 \
  -p MEMORY=2Gi \
  -p SSH_PUBLIC_KEY="$SSH_PUB_KEY" \
  | oc apply -f -
