Troubleshooting Common Issues
Template Application Errors
Issue: Template parameters not being processed correctly

Solution:

# Validate template syntax
oc process --dry-run ubuntu-basic-vm-template -p VM_NAME=test-vm

# Check for missing required parameters
oc process ubuntu-basic-vm-template --parameters
VM Creation Failures
Issue: VM fails to start or create

Solution:

# Check VM events
oc describe vm <vm-name>

# Check VMI status
oc get vmi <vm-name> -o yaml

# Check pod logs
oc logs -l kubevirt.io/domain=<vm-name>
Storage Issues
Issue: Disk provisioning failures

Solution:

# Check storage classes
oc get storageclass

# Verify PVC creation
oc get pvc

# Check available storage
oc describe nodes | grep -A5 "Allocated resources"
Network Connectivity Problems
Issue: Cannot access VM or VM cannot reach external networks

Solution:

# Check network policies
oc get networkpolicy

# Verify service mesh configuration
oc get pods -n istio-system

# Test pod network connectivity
oc run test-pod --image=busybox --rm -it -- /bin/sh
Best Practices for VM Template Management
Template Organization
• Use descriptive names that indicate the purpose and OS type • Implement consistent labeling for easy filtering and management • Version your templates using annotations or separate template names • Document template parameters thoroughly in descriptions

